@startuml fig5_overview
' Diagram 5 of the ISO/IEC 22989 pattern: everything needed to describe an AI
' system.
'
' Conventions: shared/FIGURES.md, section 7. This diagram is for the
' documentation, not for a paper, and it therefore shows the whole of the
' pattern rather than one statement. Diagrams 1 to 4 are the readable cuts
' through it.
'
' What it shows: the three views the pattern is built in, and how they connect.
'
'   1  the system, its tasks and its functions    what it is and what it does
'   2  algorithms, models and parameters          what carries the behaviour
'   3  data, its kinds and its preparation        what it runs on
'   4  qualities                                  how well it does it
'
' Left out on purpose: the leaves of three taxonomies, that is the four task
' kinds, the four learning types and the seven data process steps. Each is a
' flat fan under a class that is shown, they add nothing to the structure this
' drawing is about, and diagrams 1 to 3 carry them.
'
' Also left out: the disjointness of training, validation and evaluation data,
' which cannot be drawn without an edge between every pair. The pattern asserts
' it after the notes to 3.2.14 and 3.2.15.

skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 20
skinparam ranksep 40
skinparam padding 2
skinparam ArrowColor #1A2733
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowFontColor #1A2733
hide empty members
hide circle
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FCEFC7
  BorderColor #C9A227
  FontColor #1A2733
  FontSize 13
  BorderThickness 1
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #8A98A8
  BackgroundColor #FCFDFE
  FontColor #33475B
  FontSize 12
  FontStyle italic
}

' ===================================================================
'  1  The system, its tasks and its functions
' ===================================================================

package "What it is and what it does" {
  class AISystem
  class AIComponent
  class AIType
  class SymbolicAI
  class SubsymbolicAI
  class SystemDesign
  class Task
  class Prediction

  class AIFunction
  class Acquisition
  class Storing
  class DataProcessing
  class Training
  class Validation
  class Verification
  class Evaluation
  class Inference
  class Control

  AIType <|-- SymbolicAI
  AIType <|-- SubsymbolicAI

  AIFunction <|-- Acquisition
  AIFunction <|-- Storing
  AIFunction <|-- DataProcessing
  AIFunction <|-- Training
  AIFunction <|-- Validation
  AIFunction <|-- Verification
  AIFunction <|-- Evaluation
  AIFunction <|-- Inference
  AIFunction <|-- Control

  Acquisition -[hidden]right- Storing
  Storing -[hidden]right- DataProcessing
  DataProcessing -[hidden]right- Training
  Training -[hidden]right- Validation
  Validation -[hidden]right- Verification
  Verification -[hidden]right- Evaluation
  Evaluation -[hidden]right- Inference
  Inference -[hidden]right- Control
}

note bottom of Task
  Four kinds sit below Task,
  see diagram 1.
end note

' ===================================================================
'  2  Algorithms, models and parameters
' ===================================================================

package "What carries the behaviour" {
  class Algorithm
  class ModelAlgorithm
  class TrainingAlgorithm
  class MLAlgorithm
  class EvaluationAlgorithm
  class EvaluationMetric
  class LearningType
  class Model
  class MLModel
  class ModelParameter
  class Hyperparameter
  class MachineLearning
  class Retraining

  Algorithm <|-- ModelAlgorithm
  Algorithm <|-- TrainingAlgorithm
  Algorithm <|-- EvaluationAlgorithm
  TrainingAlgorithm <|-- MLAlgorithm
  Model <|-- MLModel

  ModelAlgorithm -[hidden]right- TrainingAlgorithm
  TrainingAlgorithm -[hidden]right- EvaluationAlgorithm
}

' ===================================================================
'  3  Data
' ===================================================================

package "What it runs on" {
  class Data
  class DataSet
  class Sample
  class Label
  class InputData
  class TrainingData
  class ValidationData
  class EvaluationData
  class ProductionData
  class DataProcess
  class DataSource
  class DataSink

  Data <|-- InputData
  Data <|-- TrainingData
  Data <|-- ValidationData
  Data <|-- EvaluationData
  Data <|-- ProductionData

  InputData -[hidden]right- TrainingData
  TrainingData -[hidden]right- ValidationData
  ValidationData -[hidden]right- EvaluationData
  EvaluationData -[hidden]right- ProductionData
}

note bottom of DataProcess
  Seven steps sit below
  DataProcess, see diagram 3.
end note

' ===================================================================
'  4  Qualities, and what reaches beyond the subdomain
' ===================================================================

package "How well it does it" {
  class CharacteristicValue
  class Characteristic
  class Controllability
  class Risk
}

' ===================================================================
'  The relations that tie the views together
' ===================================================================

AISystem --> AIComponent  : consistsOf
AISystem --> AIType       : hasType
AISystem --> SystemDesign : hasDesign
AISystem --> Task         : hasTask
AISystem --> AIFunction   : hasFunction
AIComponent --> AIFunction : hasFunction
AIComponent --> Model      : realisedByModel

Inference  --> Prediction : creates
Prediction --> Task       : fulfilsTask
Inference  --> Model      : isExecutedBy

Model     --> Algorithm      : basedOnAlgorithm
Model     --> ModelParameter : hasParameter
Algorithm --> Hyperparameter : hasHyperparameter
Hyperparameter --> CharacteristicValue : hasSetting
MLAlgorithm --> LearningType : basedOnLearning
Training  --> ModelParameter : determines
MLModel   --> Training       : isCreatedBy
Training <|-- MachineLearning
Training <|-- Retraining
EvaluationAlgorithm --> EvaluationMetric : usesMetric

AIFunction --> Data       : usesData
DataSet    --> Data       : isComposedOf
Data       --> Sample     : isComposedOf
Sample     --> Label      : hasLabel
Data       --> DataProcess : isProcessedBy
Acquisition --> DataSource : hasDataSource
Storing     --> DataSink   : hasDataSink

AISystem --> CharacteristicValue : hasCharacteristicValue
CharacteristicValue --> Characteristic : forCharacteristic
AISystem --> Controllability : hasControllability
AISystem --> Risk            : hasRisk

@enduml
